  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x200b;Developing a Comprehensive Reparations Legal and Policy Framework for Survivors of Conflict-Related Sexual Violence&#x200b;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to endow the Government with context-specific tools, knowledge, and a strategy to develop and implement inclusive, timely, and effective policies and legal frameworks that ensure the provision of reparations to conflict-affected populations. To achieve this, IOM and its partners propose to provide expert advice and technical assistance to the Government to develop a consultative platform and a comprehensive reparations framework for victims of human rights violations, including conflict-related sexual violence survivors. In particular, the proposed intervention focuses on the first goal defined by the Implementation Plan: the development of a reparations legal and policy framework and consultative platform to inform the design of comprehensive reparations laws, policies, and mechanisms by the end of 2022.</narrative>
  </description>
